    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The casting decision for Lupita Nyong'o as Helen of Troy and Clytemnestra ignited a fierce digital backlash. This online criticism escalated into a public accusation by gatekeepers who weaponized heritage, framing the move as erasing European history. The resulting conflict has exposed a schism over cultural ownership, turning the mythic epic into a flashpoint for a revealed power struggle over who may claim classical stories in mass-market film.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
